disruptorC

C implementation of LMAX's disruptor pattern.

Tested on Mac OS X 10.8.3 (gcc 4.8.0), Fedora 18, and FreeBSD 10.0 (clang 3.3).

Build by:

      ./bootstrap 
      make

Then run the tests in test/.


Multi-producer vs single-producer

* publisher_next_entry_* / publisher_commit_entry_*
  Multi-producer. Claiming uses a fetch-add (or CAS). Publishing
  marks available[seq] and does not wait for earlier publishers.

* sp_publisher_next_entry_* / sp_publisher_commit_entry
  Single-producer only. Plain increment plus a release store of
  max_read_cursor. Do not mix with the multi-producer claim functions
  on the same ring.

* publisher_next_entries_* / sp_publisher_next_entries_*
  Claim n slots. cursor->sequence is the last sequence in the range
  [cursor->sequence - n + 1, cursor->sequence].

Entries are unpadded by default (DEFINE_ENTRY_TYPE). Use
DEFINE_PADDED_ENTRY_TYPE if neighbouring slots false-share.

Wait knobs (define before including disruptor.h):

* DISRUPTOR_PAUSE_SPINS   — PAUSE iterations between condition checks
                             (default 64). BUILTIN_WAIT_COUNT__ is an alias.
* DISRUPTOR_YIELD_EVERY   — wait ticks before sched_yield() (default 32).


NOTES:

* Now using the __atomic* operations as supported in GCC 4.7.1
  onwards.
